  "instruction": "You are given an OpenFAST linearization template.\nComplete the following from the command line:\n\n1. Modify the main file `/home/user/Desktop/linear.fst`:\n- Set `Linearize=True`\n- Set `CalcSteady=True`\n- Set `NLinTimes=1`\n- Set `LinInputs=0`, `LinOutputs=0` (or as needed)\n- Set `TMax=60` (ensure linearization after reaching steady state)\n\n2. Run `openfast linear` to generate `/home/user/Desktop/linear.lin` and `/home/user/Desktop/linear.out`.\n\n3. Write a post-processing script to parse the `.lin` file (or extract from `.out`):\n- Extract the state matrix `A` (or directly use OpenFAST post-processing scripts)\n- Compute eigenvalues and identify first-order tower fore-aft and side-side mode frequencies (about 0.32 Hz)\n- Save to `/home/user/Desktop/summary.txt` in this format: `tower_fa_freq_hz, tower_ss_freq_hz`\n\n4. Do not use GUI tools.\n\n[Init Package Note]\n- Additional initialization dependencies are pre-uploaded under `/home/user/Desktop` (or `C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\Desktop` on Windows) with relative structure preserved.\n- Continue following the original task workflow: generate/modify required files and compute outputs yourself.\n- Only initialization inputs are included; no answer/result artifacts are preloaded.\n",
